findings.finding:
The plan deliberately changes what failure some calls surface on Windows: undecodable output now raises UnicodeDecodeError instead of yielding garbled text. It never states the disposition of that new failure arm. Specifically, it does not say:
- whether the exception propagates as an uncaught traceback or is mapped by callers;
- whether that outcome is fatal or permanent for the operation;
- whether call sites whose handlers catch only CalledProcessError/OSError will let it escape as a crash.
The phrase 'surfaces corrupt output' names an intent, not what the caller (CLI user, MCP client, library caller) actually sees.
